{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_u5jtwxmunptc3hwuluvprufynbs4lwv3wn65at7iurm5pso7lk4a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. All four phases done.\n\n## What the library is\n\nThe entire C library is 13 lines: one exported function `hdr_compare(const uint8_t *h1, const uint8_t *h2)` plus a `static` helper `hdr_valid` — an MP3 frame-header validity/compatibility check.\n\n## Phase A — surface mapped (artifacts in crate root)\n\n| artifact | content |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` | C `.so` exports exactly **one** symbol, `hdr_compare`; Rust `.so` exports it too. Symbol diff empty. `hdr_valid` is `static` → exported by neither. Both C source files fully translated, no skipped module, no stubs. |\n| `ERRORS.md` | **16 rows**, grepped mechanically from every rejection site (5 `hdr_valid` gates, 3 `hdr_compare` gates, 5 read-extent/short-circuit contracts, out-of-range enum sweep, combined-failure row). Documents the deliberate non-checks so Rust isn't \"fixed\" (`h1` is never validated, `h1[0]` never read, CRC/padding/private bits masked out). |\n| `CONFIGS.md` | **22 rows** over the axes the C branches on (3 sync forms, 4 layer codes, 16 bitrate indices incl. free-format and reserved, 4 sample-rate codes, masked-out bits, aliasing, overlap, misalignment, read extent). **No `[features]` in Cargo.toml and no `option()` in CMakeLists → exactly 1 valid feature combination** (the empty set); both Cargo profiles verified because `release` sets `panic=\"abort\"`. |\n\n## Phases B–D — 37 differential tests, all through `libloading`\n\nBoth libraries are `dlopen`ed and called via their exported `hdr_compare`; the Rust code is never called directly.\n\n- **Complete input-space proof** (row 22): `hdr_compare` reads at most 5 bytes, so all **2³² combinations** of `h1[1]×h1[2]×h2[1]×h2[2]` with `h2[0]=0xff` were enumerated (8-way sharded, ~20 s), plus 2²⁴ sweeps for six `h2[0]≠0xff` values. This is exhaustive, not sampled.\n- **Read-extent contract** (`tests/read_extent.rs`): guard-page mappings + `NULL` prove Rust dereferences exactly the bytes C does, on every short-circuit path — run in a child process, with a self-check test that *must* crash to prove the guard pages have teeth.\n- **Symbol parity enforced as a test** (`tests/symbols.rs`), re-deriving `nm -D` at test time.\n- `./verify.sh` automates it all: enumerates the feature power set from `Cargo.toml`, builds the C `.so`, then runs check/build/test + `nm -D` diff per combination × profile.\n\n## Test suite validated by mutation testing\n\nPassing tests are worthless if they can't fail, so I injected **14 mutants** into `src/lib.rs` (mask changes, reserved-value changes, XOR→AND, return `1`→`2`, and five short-circuit/read-order violations). **All 14 were caught; 0 survivors.** The five read-order mutants were caught *only* by the guard-page test — the class of bug happy-path tests miss entirely. Source restored byte-identical afterwards (md5 verified).\n\n## Result\n\n**No divergences found; `src/lib.rs` needed no changes** — the translation was already exactly correct, and that is now proven over the entire reachable input space rather than asserted. Final clean-slate run: `cargo clean` + `rm -rf c_src/build` → **37/37 tests passing in both profiles, empty symbol diff, exit 0**. Nothing in `c_src/` was modified (md5s unchanged; only the `build/` dir was created as instructed)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1253,"cache_read_input_tokens":131545,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1253,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9f595d59-0c25-4dea-9ef2-252193c84ef7","uuid":"0ac53bea-1236-48ab-82e4-dc8cbf8b6254","timestamp":"2026-08-19T15:35:11.796Z"}
